  "anomaly_detected": false,
  "confidence": 0.8,
  "anomalies": [],
  "summary": "Systematic review of the netlist and SPICE deck against the specification found the build functionally consistent with the intended design: the 24 V path (fuse F2, TVS D1, plus a P-FET reverse-polarity switch T8 whose gate is self-biased on by R52/D5), the TPS62933 buck (R31/R32 feedback giving ~5 V), the AZ1117 LDO, both ADM3260 isolated pH/EC channels (isolated grounds/domains kept separate, PDIS shared on IO6, VSEL divider identical on both), the three TMC2209 drivers (six 110 mΩ sense resistors, 14k/10.7k VREF dividers from per-driver 5VOUT, distinct UART addresses, STEP lines on IO11/IO15/IO19, shared UART on IO21/IO22 through 1k), the main-pump and ATO-valve switches with float-switch interlocks, and the I2C/float/actuator pin map all match the spec's stated values and topology. The spec's reference designators (M1/M2, U1–U7, T1–T5, R1/R3/R4, etc.) are shifted relative to this netlist, but every function and value the spec describes is present and correctly wired; the unwired TF-Luna, DNP BME280/BH1750, and firmware GPIO mismatch are documented known limitations, not board anomalies."
}

